-- title:
--   Three-torsion projection from nongeneration
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be an abelian group. Let $a,d,h\in G$ satisfy $2h=0$, $3d\in\{0,h\}$, $\langle a,d,h\rangle=G$, and $\langle a,h\rangle\ne G$. There exists an additive endomorphism $p:G\to G$ such that
--
--   $$p^2=p,\qquad 3p(x)=0\ (x\in G),\qquad p(a)=p(h)=0,\qquad p(d)=-2d.$$
--
--   This provides the projection used to construct a reflection.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, https://github.com/alexcour/couret-finite-verifications/blob/65b828d9ffd016ce2a1b05403f303fa5f948c10f/research/correspondants_20261013/lean/CayleyTwoColourAbelian.lean#L671-L701, lines 671–701; source file SHA-256 c9643d6e3a677d5a903623825d50a309d87175a21ace2b7ab56939d9189f13b1; theorem Couret.CayleyDoublet.abelianThreeProjection_of_nongeneration

